          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Which of the following causes massive splenomegaly (spleen weight exceeding one </p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which of the following causes massive splenomegaly (spleen weight exceeding one kilogram)?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Autoimmune haemolytic anaemia</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>AIHA causes moderate splenomegaly through Fc-receptor-mediated clearance of IgG-coated red blood cells. It does not produce massive enlargement.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Infective endocarditis</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Infective endocarditis causes mild reactive enlargement or small abscesses from septic emboli, but not massive splenomegaly.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Gaucher disease</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Gaucher disease (glucocerebrosidase deficiency) is one of the six classic causes of massive splenomegaly, alongside CML, myelofibrosis, kala-azar, chronic malaria, and thalassaemia major.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Niemann-Pick disease</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Niemann-Pick disease (sphingomyelinase deficiency) typically causes moderate splenomegaly with prominent neurological features, not massive enlargement.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Of these choices, only Gaucher disease causes massive splenomegaly. AIHA and Niemann-Pick cause moderate enlargement; endocarditis causes mild. Remember the six: CML, myelofibrosis, kala-azar, chronic malaria, Gaucher, thalassaemia major."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. Gaucher disease produces massive splenomegaly through glucocerebroside accumulation in macrophages. The six causes: CML, myelofibrosis, kala-azar, chronic malaria, Gaucher, and thalassaemia major."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
